// Aims and objectives
- Our goal is to deliver a reliable, intuitive, and course-specific astronomy
  learning tool that enhances the learning experience for ASTRO 100 students.
- At the same time, the tool will support teaching staff in delivering
  interactive lab content in the course.
- We also aim to create lasting value by ensuring that OPIS can be maintained
  and can continue to be used in the future of ASTRO 100.

// Target audience
- ASTRO 100 is an introductory astronomy course offered at the University of
  Auckland / Waipapa Taumata Rau, with both science and general education
  streams.
- Students enrolled in ASTRO 100 come from a wide range of academic backgrounds
  within the University, and have varying levels of technical knowledge, both in
  the domain of the subject, as well as with using technical tools.

